<title>CHINA: Shanghai exchange sets rules for holiday repos.</title>
<headline>Shanghai exchange sets rules for holiday repos.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-01-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Shanghai Securities Exchange on Saturday announced rules for the redemption of state debt re-purchase papers coming due during the Chinese lunar new year holiday.</p>
<p>The exchange said in a notice published in the Shanghai Securities News that three-month and six-month repo papers falling due during the holiday period would be settled on the first day the banks re-open.</p>
<p>The exchange is closed for two weeks from Feb 3 to 14, but banks will be closed for a much shorter period.</p>
<p>Repo papers falling due after the exchange begins its holiday but before the banks close for the festival will be settled as usual on a day-by-day basis.</p>
</text>
